  "market_context": "The market was in a clear downtrend. Price formed a double top at a resistance level, then briefly broke above it (fake out), before reversing downward—indicating bearish momentum resumption.",
  "key_observation": "In a downtrend, a fake out above a double top resistance signals the start of renewed bearish momentum, offering a high-probability short entry opportunity.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identify the dominant market direction as a clear downtrend.",
    "Step 2: Locate a double top pattern forming at a resistance area within that downtrend.",
    "Step 3: Observe price breaking above the resistance (fake out), then quickly returning below it.",
    "Step 4: Interpret the fake out as confirmation of bearish momentum and a signal to enter a short position."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Combining market direction with fake out patterns increases trade probability; a fake out above resistance in a downtrend confirms sellers are in control and provides a precise short entry trigger.",
